      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "7. Perform a factory reset on the Zenith Smart Hub by pressing and holding the recessed reset button for a minimum of fifteen seconds until the status LED flashes red three times.\n8. After the reset completes, wait five minutes for the hub to reinitialize its network stack and attempt to reconnect to the local network automatically.\n9. If the automated reconnection fails, utilize the Zenith companion mobile application to initiate a guided network setup wizard, ensuring you select the correct frequency band (2.4GHz vs. 5GHz) during configuration.\n10. Check for any known firmware updates by visiting the official Zenith support portal and manually downloading and installing the latest stable build onto the hub via a USB connection, if available.\n11. Test connectivity using a different, known-working device (like a smartphone or laptop) on the same local network to isolate whether the issue is specific to the Zenith Hub or a broader network outage.\n12. Review the hub's internal system logs (accessible through the advanced diagnostics menu) for specific error codes preceding the \"Error 404\" message, as this provides deeper diagnostic insight.\n13. If all preceding steps fail, attempt to change the DHCP lease time settings on your",
